  "details": "Description\n\nWhen launching VRChat in PC mode, all avatars, including both Public and Private avatars, appear as the default error robot. Resetting User Data temporarily restores the avatars to their normal appearance, but the issue returns every time the game is launched.\n\nThe Worlds menu also displays an incorrect label, showing \"H3\" instead of \"My Worlds\", and previously saved or favorited content is missing.\n\nThe same issues occur in both PCVR mode and Quest standalone mode.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\nLaunch VRChat in PC mode.\n\nObserve that all Public and Private avatars appear as error robots.\n\nOpen the Worlds menu and check the \"My Worlds\" section.\n\nObserve that the section label displays \"H3\" and previously saved content is missing.\n\nReset User Data and relaunch the game.\n\nObserve that avatars may temporarily return to normal, but the issue recurs after launching the game again.\n\nRepeat the process in PCVR mode or Quest standalone mode and observe the same issues.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: 其他\n\n- Frequency: 總是\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.3.3p2-1921-15c4a824b2-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report\n\n---\n\n**Log file:** [output_log_2026-10-18_23-21-53.txt](https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/file/file_88176031-789d-4981-abcd-556a07613d7d/1/file)",
